// Module 3 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 3

::M3 Q1:: Which split should you use to tune hyperparameters? {
~Test set
~Training set only
=Validation set#Tune on validation data. Keep the test set for one final, honest score.
~Any, it does not matter
}

::M3 Q2:: Which is a sign of overfitting? {
~Training and validation loss both high
~Both losses equal
~Loss is exactly zero on validation
=Training loss low, validation loss rising#The model is memorizing the training data, so it does worse on new data.
}

::M3 Q3:: What does early stopping do? {
~Stops the GPU
=Stops training when validation performance stops improving#It ends training once validation stops improving and keeps the best checkpoint.
~Removes layers
~Doubles the batch size
}

::M3 Q4:: Why track experiments? {
=To compare runs and reproduce results#Logging settings and metrics lets you compare runs fairly and recreate the best one.
~To reduce model size
~To speed up inference
~To label data
}

::M3 Q5:: Which technique reduces overfitting? {
~Using the test set for tuning
~Removing validation data
=Dropout#Dropout randomly switches off units during training so the model cannot rely on any single one.
~Training longer with no checks
}
